  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "S2 sets a 7% permanent failure cap with no sales stop, existing models exempt from nothing, and per-model results to customers, which keeps the Hearth 10 (6.2%) under the cap but exceeds the 5% benchmark. S5 makes recall non-automatic at 8 per 100,000: the threshold triggers notice, a corrective-action plan, and independent review, with recall only on confirmed ongoing serious risk or failed correction, and corrective action has no time bound. S1 (24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents) and S4 (suppression within 36 months) are close to the acceptable range."
 },
